# Bit-test (, 2026-09-25): tip4pfq_gas with ACKS2 bond-softness (`bondsoft 1.0 2.0`: kappa 1.0, bcut 2.0 A), which
# arms the inter-site kappa block, selects the MINRES saddle solver and the Gaussian taper H. No case covered it before
# (uninit_reads_s86). tests/perturb.sh covers it at np 2.
# Bit-test: TIP4P-FQ 4-site (M-site) single molecule, short-range gated solve.
# Pins the 4-site augmented-X path (charge on H + massless M, oxygen excluded from
# the fq group) — the TIP4P-FQ solver that the long-standing blocker lives in.
units           metal
atom_style      full
boundary        f f f
region          box block -20 20 -20 20 -20 20
create_box      3 box
mass            1 15.9994
mass            2 1.008
mass            3 1.0e-6
molecule        h2o water4.mol
create_atoms    0 single 0.0 0.0 0.0 mol h2o 1
group           fq type 2 3
pair_style      lj/cut/coul/cut 12.0
pair_coeff      1 1 0.0124 3.159
pair_coeff      2 2 0.0 1.0
pair_coeff      3 3 0.0 1.0
neighbor        2.0 bin
fix             chg fq qeq/sam 1 0.0 12.0 1.0e-9 water4.param
fix_modify      chg bondsoft 1.0 2.0
run             0
variable        peval equal pe
print           "${peval}" file pe.txt screen no
write_dump      all custom charges.dump id type q modify sort id format line "%d %d %.12g"
